<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ CPI fell 0.3 pct Mar qtr, rose 1.8 pct Mar yr.</title>
<headline>NZ CPI fell 0.3 pct Mar qtr, rose 1.8 pct Mar yr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Tuesday released the following data on the Consumers Price Index to March 1997.</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter changes -</p>
<p>    Mar 1997		    Dec 1996		  Mar 1996</p>
<p>    -0.3 pct		    +0.7 pct		  +0.5 pct</p>
<p>Year-on-year changes -</p>
<p>    Mar 1997		    Dec 1996		  Mar 1996</p>
<p>    +1.8 pct		    +2.6 pct		  +2.2 pct</p>
<p>Qtr-on-qtr ex-housing and credit services -</p>
<p>    Mar 1997		    Dec 1996		  Mar 1996</p>
<p>    +0.1 pct		    +0.7 pct		  +0.4 pct</p>
<p>Year-on-year ex-housing and credit services -</p>
<p>    Mar 1997		    Dec 1996		  Mar 1996</p>
<p>    +1.7 pct		    +2.0 pct		  +1.3 pct</p>
<p>All groups excluding central and local govt charges (annual)</p>
<p>    Mar 1997		    Dec 1996		  Mar 1996</p>
<p>    +1.5 pct		    +2.3 pct		  +1.8 pct</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand (RBNZ) in its March economic projections forecast CPI inflation at 0.1 percent in the March quarter and 2.2 percent on an annual basis.  </p>
<p>Fourteen economists polled by Reuters predicted on average a 0.11 percent quarterly CPI rise, for an annual increase of 2.19 percent.</p>
<p>Contributions of commodity groups to CPI quarterly movements:</p>
<p>				    Mar 1997	Dec 1996    Mar 1996</p>
<p>    Food			    0.7		0.6	   0.0</p>
<p>    Housing			 0.3		0.7	   1.3</p>
<p>    Household operation	 0.2		0.5	   0.3</p>
<p>    Apparel			-1.1		0.7	  -0.6</p>
<p>    Transport		    -0.9		0.6	  -0.4</p>
<p>    Tobacco/Alcohol	     0.7		0.6	   1.5</p>
<p>    Personal &amp; health care    0.5		1.7	   1.0</p>
<p>    Recreation, education     0.9	     -0.2	   2.2</p>
<p>    Credit services	    -5.4		0.9	  -1.7</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4 4734746)</p>
</text>
